    {
      "class_code": 22,
      "payload": {
        "name": "pc-check-retry-eligibility",
        "description": "Deterministic pure-logic guard that decides whether a Tool invocation is eligible for a bounded retry, before any retry is considered. It performs evidence-conditioned logic only: it does not grant dispatch permission, does not reset attempt counts, and does not replay completed effects. Returns retry: true only when outcome is exactly 'retryable', operation_state is not 'completed', attempt < max_attempts (both positive integers), and read_only or dedup_verified is true. Any missing, null, or invalid input fails closed with retry: false; it never raises. Completed effects never replay even when read_only or dedup_verified is true. This guard is a reusable building block for Recipe/usage failure contracts; it never bypasses current instance-wide Tool policy, cancellation, stale-attempt fencing, or resource limits, and it assumes the typed inputs mapping and Monty runner support are implemented on the selected path.",
        "content": "operation_state = inputs[\"operation_state\"]\noutcome = inputs[\"outcome\"]\nattempt = inputs[\"attempt\"]\nmax_attempts = inputs[\"max_attempts\"]\nread_only = inputs[\"read_only\"]\ndedup_verified = inputs[\"dedup_verified\"]\n\nretry = (\n    outcome == \"retryable\"\n    and operation_state != \"completed\"\n    and isinstance(attempt, int) and not isinstance(attempt, bool)\n    and isinstance(max_attempts, int) and not isinstance(max_attempts, bool)\n    and 0 < attempt < max_attempts\n    and (read_only is True or dedup_verified is True)\n)\n\nresult = {\"retry\": bool(retry)}"
